    {
      "receiptId": "bacon-pudding-hampshire.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "The original source of this receipt isn\u0027t known. Can you help? \u003Ca href=\u0022mailto:editor@foodsofengland.co.uk?subject=Foods%20of%20England,%20Bacon%20Pudding%20-%20Hampshire\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003Eeditor@foodsofengland.co.uk\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E",
      "receiptText": "8 oz plain flour\u003Cbr\u003E\n1 tsp Baking powder\u003Cbr\u003E\n4 oz shredded suet\u003Cbr\u003E\nwater to mix\u003Cbr\u003E\n8 rashers bacon, chopped\u003Cbr\u003E\n1 onion, chopped\u003Cbr\u003E\n1 tsp chopped sage\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nSift the flour, baking powder and salt into a bowl, add the suet and enough water to bind into a soft dough. Roll out the dough into an oblong. Cover with the onions and bacon, leaving a margin clear around the edge, sprinkle with the sage, salt and pepper. Dampen the edges and roll up. Tie in a cloth and boil for 2 hours, or steam wrapped in greaseproof paper for 3 hours.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
